what high-level and doesn't enumerate all sub-requirements of Article 12(3). But as a commitment to build infrastructure, it hits the right target. The specific implementation details (which exact events to log for which system category) would be worked out during development.\n\nI think this clears my bar. It's a direct compliance enabler that reduces institutional risk significantly. I'd approve it. Promise score: high — maybe 82-85. It's very well-aligned with what I need, but the high-level nature means there are implementation risks (will they actually cover all of Art 12(3)(a)-(d)? Will they handle the lifetime persistence requirement? Will modular wrappers work across truly diverse architectures?). These uncertainties prevent me from giving it a 95+. But it's clearly worth pursuing.\n\nLet me settle on 84 — strong alignment, clear regulatory value, but implementation details need to nail specific sub-requirements.\n",
