ile the direction is right and the core obligation is mandatory (so building something like this is not optional), there are gaps in specificity for Art 12(2) and 12(3), scope issues, and single-point-of-failure concerns. It's a solid foundation but needs refinement.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The obligation under Art 12(1) is MANDATORY. We must have automatic logging for high-risk systems. This proposal directly builds the infrastructure to fulfill that obligation. From my compliance perspective, this is not optional - we need something like this. The fact that it's a centralized, automated approach rather than per-project ad-hoc solutions reduces our risk profile significantly.\n\nI'll approve with a score around 72-78. It's directionally correct and addresses the core mandatory requirement, but has notable gaps in addressing the full scope of Art 12(2) and (3), and some implementation risks that could undermine rather than support compliance if not addressed.\n",
