ing gate would significantly impede our iteration speed.\n\nDecision: I'm leaning toward reject. The proposal addresses a tangential concern (documentation currency) rather than the actual technical obligation in Article 12 (automatic logging). And its implementation mechanism (blocking merges with human sign-off) directly conflicts with prototyping velocity. It's a governance process, not a technical engineering solution to the record-keeping requirement.\n\nPromise score: From my vantage point, maybe 30-35. The underlying principle is sound but it doesn't solve the actual problem and would hurt our speed. I'll say 32.\n",
