rk. The scoping to \"prototyping phase\" keeps it proportionate.\n\nThe main risk is scope creep in what \"flags anomalies based on Article 12 criteria\" means, but the core value proposition (centralized log visualization replacing manual review) is clear and cost-effective.\n\nI'd say this clears my bar. It's efficient use of resources, doesn't require speculative funding, leverages existing infrastructure patterns, and directly serves R&D productivity. I'd give it a solid score — maybe 72-78. Not a 90+ because there are some scope ambiguities and the \"real-time\" + \"across all active systems\" framing could lead to over-engineering if not carefully scoped in implementation.\n\nLet me settle on 74 — solid approval from my vantage point, with minor caveats about scope definition.\n",
