cal compliance\" is a bit strong as wording (compliance involves more than just logging), but the substance of what's proposed is well-aligned with Article 12 and efficiently scoped. The resource-efficiency argument is very strong here.\n\nDecision: approve\nPromise: I'd rate this highly — maybe 85-90. It's a clear win on resource efficiency, it's well-scoped, it leverages existing infrastructure, and it directly reduces the per-project compliance burden that would otherwise eat into research time. The only reason I'm not at 100 is the slight overclaim in \"guarantees\" and the need to ensure the upfront development effort doesn't become a sunk cost if requirements shift (though the EU AI Act is now law, so that risk is low).\n\nI'll go with 87.\n",
