vestment that benefits multiple compliance areas.\n\nBut it's not THE thing Article 12 is asking for. The operational logging system (event recording during deployment) is what's legally required by Article 12(1)-(3). This proposal addresses development provenance, which is more under Annex IV technical documentation.\n\nI think I'll approve at a moderate level — say 55-60. It's useful complementary infrastructure that supports the compliance program broadly, and the cryptographic hashing provides auditability. But it's not a direct Article 12 implementation. From my vantage point, it's supporting but not critical. It helps with market reputation (demonstrable traceability to regulators) and institutional survival (audit readiness).\n\nLet me settle on: approve, promise 58. It's genuinely useful for the compliance ecosystem and supports traceability requirements, but it addresses a different part of the regulatory picture than what Article 12 most directly demands.\n",
