tion requires specific structured data fields that are operational, not architectural.\n- Speed of prototyping: extremely slow. This is a multi-year research project at best.\n- Quality of output for the actual regulatory requirement: poor fit.\n\nI would reject this. It's an interesting research direction in XAI but it doesn't address what Article 12 actually requires, and from a development/engineering standpoint, the practical solution (structured event logging) is trivially prototypable compared to this.\n\nPromise score: From my vantage point, this proposal has very low promise for meeting the regulatory requirement through feasible engineering. The research might be interesting academically but it's not a viable path to compliance. I'd give it maybe 8-12. It shows some creative thinking but fundamentally misdiagnoses the problem and proposes an infeasible solution timeline. Let me say 10.\n",
