e.\n\nI think this clears my bar with reservations. The technical approach is viable, the API wrapper pattern is standard and well-understood, and once built it would genuinely help prototyping speed for new systems. The concerns about \"ledger\" over-engineering and scope ambiguity are real but addressable in implementation. I'd approve it but not give it a super-high score because of the scope ambiguity and potential over-engineering risk.\n\nDecision: Approve\nPromise: Around 72-75. It's technically viable, the pattern is well-understood, it would help prototyping speed once built, but the \"immutable centralized ledger\" language suggests some over-engineering risk, and the scope description has a gap between what's described (Annex III 1(a) fields) and what's claimed (all high-risk systems).\n",
